om https://github.com/goodfeli/dlbook_notation.\n\\input{math_commands.tex}\n\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{url}\n\n\n\\title{Formatting Instructions for ICLR 2026 \\\\ Conference Submissions}\n\n% Authors must not appear in the submitted version. They should be hidden\n% as long as the \\iclrfinalcopy macro remains commented out below.\n% Non-anonymous submissions will be rejected without review.\n\n\\author{Antiquus S.~Hippocampus, Natalia Cerebro \\& Amelie P. Amygdale \\thanks{ Use footnote for providing further information\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:3:\\usepackage{iclr2026_conference,times}\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:12:\\title{Formatting Instructions for ICLR 2026 \\\\ Conference Submissions}\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:15:% as long as the \\iclrfinalcopy macro remains commented out below.\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:18:\\author{Antiquus S.~Hippocampus, Natalia Cerebro \\& Amelie P. Amygdale \\thanks{ Use footnote for providing further information\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:19:about author (webpage, alternative address)---\\emph{not} for acknowledging\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:32:Coauthor \\\\\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:38:% The \\author macro works with any number of authors. There are two commands\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:39:% used to separate the names and addresses of multiple authors: \\And and \\AND.\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:41:% Using \\And between authors leaves it to \\LaTeX{} to determine where to break\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:43:% puts 3 of 4 authors names on the first line, and the last on the second\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:44:% line, try using \\AND instead of \\And before the third author name.\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:49:%\\iclrfinalcopy % Uncomment for camera-ready version, but NOT for submission.\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:63:\\section{Submission of conference papers to ICLR 2026}\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:69:  {\\textbackslash}iclrfinalcopy} should be inserted to adjust the\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:78:Papers to be submitted to ICLR 2026 must be prepared according to the\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:97:The file \\verb+iclr2026_conference.pdf+ contains these\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:101:\\verb+iclr2026_conference.sty+ and \\verb+iclr2026_conference.bst+ (to be used with \\LaTeX{}2e). The file\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:102:\\verb+iclr2026_conference.tex+ may be used as a ``shell'' for writing your paper. All you\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:103:have to do is replace the author, title, abstract, and text of the paper with\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:123:address. The lead author's name is to be listed first, and\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:124:the co-authors' names are set to follow. Authors sharing the\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:160:and include the authors' last names and year (with the ``et~al.'' construct\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:161:for more than two authors). When the authors or the publication are\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:168:authors, in the \\textsc{References} section. As to the format of the\n/tmp/iclr2026_conference.tex:398:If you'd like to, you may include  a section for author contributions as is done\n1e63a67dbf6bf6aa973471e5e4b45425afa734bf52c569de2a25161f77b93493  source_evidence/evaluate_final.py\nsha256:1e63a67dbf6bf6aa973471e5e4b45425afa734bf52c569de2a25161f77b93493\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
