{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-\\\\paragraph{Implementation and qualification boundaries.}\n+\\\\paragraph{Decision reliability is a separate target.}\n+The evaluation also records whether the protected-report comparison with the all-question default score has the opposite strict sign to the reference accuracy comparison. In notation, it checks\n+\"'$'\"\\\\mathbf{1}\\\\{(\\\\widehat p_{\\\\rm protect}-\\\\overline X_{\\\\cdot1})(a_{\\\\widehat j}-a_1)<0\\\\}\"'$,\n+where $a$ denotes known truth in simulation or observed audit accuracy for real questions. Ties do not count as disagreements; they remain in the averaging denominator. In the real sixteen-prompt conditions, this diagnostic is one in four of five seeds at $n=64$ and one of five at $n=256$. Thus a lower reporting MSE does not ensure a stable directional comparison on the observed samples. However, the diagnostic mixes a protected selected-prompt report with an all-question fixed-prompt report, and its real reference is itself noisy. It is not the probability that a naive superiority claim is overturned, does not compare two independently trained systems, and supplies no population decision-error guarantee. Reporting the exact comparison is more informative than calling every sign change a failed optimization.\n+% @evidence[[analysis/summary.json#/condition_means/R64K16/decision_reversal_rate]]\n+% @evidence[[analysis/summary.json#/condition_means/R256K16/decision_reversal_rate]]\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L779]]\n+\n+'\"\\\\paragraph{Implementation and qualification boundaries.}\n*** Update File: build_claims.py\n@@\n     add('Eight of ten K=16 selected-minus-fixed audit intervals include zero; both positive exclusions are seed 5059. All K=1 paired differences are identically zero. All ten K=16 report intervals contain the finite audit reference; one K=1 real interval does not.',\n@@\n         ['final.evidence.episodes'], ['analysis/summary.json#/audit_differences', 'analysis/condition_results.csv'])\n+    add('The strict sign-disagreement diagnostic compares protected selected-prompt report minus all-question fixed score with the reference selected-minus-fixed accuracy. Four of five real K16 seeds at n64 and one of five at n256 disagree. Ties contribute zero while remaining in the denominator; this is not a naive-claim reversal probability.',\n+        ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.decision_reversal_rate'],\n+        ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L779', 'analysis/summary.json#/condition_means'])\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython build_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
